Z||000000||William Federle||09-02-2000||08:54 PM||||I just got two new calipers and new left and right parking brake cables and new pads and tried to make the parking brake work. I tightened the lever arm to the torque in the Haynes book but that makes them too tight for the spring to push them back when the parking brake is released. There must be something that the Haynes book doesn't mention but I can't figure out what it is.<P>Can someone point me in the right direction?||||reg||1
